Register the two recovered sprite-table rasterizers in the dispatch map

FUN_0041eeec / FUN_0041fa30 are referenced by the second poly-handler table region
(0x462d94..0x462ef4, entries 0x462e24/28 and 0x462ed4/d8) but Ghidra had no function
objects there -> dd2_relocate left the raw x86 addresses -> L10 execute-fault @0x41eeec.
Created via CreateMissingFns.java (project DB), re-exported (make decompile: 950 fns),
re-assembled; this patch adds their relocation-map entries.

--- a/dd2_dispatch.c
+++ b/dd2_dispatch.c
@@ -490,6 +490,8 @@
 extern int Load_Game_Vags();
 extern int Clear_SoundFx();
 extern int FUN_00448368();
+extern int FUN_0041eeec();
+extern int FUN_0041fa30();
 extern int FUN_00448e50();
 extern int PitOut();
 extern int PitIn();
@@ -1356,6 +1358,8 @@
 {0x00448310,(void*)&Load_Game_Vags},
 {0x00448364,(void*)&Clear_SoundFx},
 {0x00448368,(void*)&FUN_00448368},
+{0x0041eeec,(void*)&FUN_0041eeec},
+{0x0041fa30,(void*)&FUN_0041fa30},
 {0x00448e50,(void*)&FUN_00448e50},
 {0x00448e58,(void*)&PitOut},
 {0x00448e88,(void*)&PitIn},
